# What the system does during session.input (tests/t1/museum_editor_tools.sh). A tick is a pass of the event loop: a frame of the editor
# is one or two of them, so the event of tick T arrives between the frames T/2 and T, and session.input leaves those frames free.
# The answers of the three context menus, in the order they open.
0 dialog-answer openTable
0 dialog-answer openTable
0 dialog-answer selectAll
# The menu bar. The storyboard: Arrange > Align top, then Distribute horizontally.
10 menu-click arrange:top
12 menu-click arrange:across
# A table: Align left; later Align top.
64 menu-click arrange:left
144 menu-click arrange:top
# Another table: Centre vertically. Then a file is dropped on the window.
340 menu-click arrange:middle
342 drop @TMP@/outside/estampe.png
